Issue briefs

1. Section-path / UUID-format chunking

- Source: `section-path-issue-discussion.md`
- Main point: the current fix target is section-based chunk granularity and full section-label preservation, while keeping current Generator/Turbine span and ESN logic unchanged.
- Scope update from 2026-09-14: among about 18,340 `36UUID` docs, only 29 appear to have bad or missing TOC handling, and only 3 of those seem materially important.
- Practical implication: this is still priority 1 because it affects chunk quality and retrieval behavior, but the latest direction is to fix chunk granularity and full section labels in the main path first and not build a separate UUID no-TOC fallback right now.

2. Final master report

- Sources: `section-path-issue-discussion.md`, `final-master-report-retrieval-note.md`
- Main point: `final_master_report` is large enough to justify its own preprocessing profile and may also need a dedicated retrieval review.
- Practical implication: this should stay high priority because it sits directly in the second priority bucket and also overlaps with the ambiguity notes.

3. Versioned / legacy docs

- Source: `section-path-issue-discussion.md`
- Main point: version-based docs and older legacy docs look structurally different from UUID-format docs and appear to need their own preprocess path.
- Practical implication: treat this as a designable family-level fix, not a one-off patch.

4. Missing docs in QA

- Source: `missing_docs_post_2016`
- Main point: this is not one single failure mode. One doc is simply pending chunking in QA, while the other should never have been expected in QA because it is from a dev-only source path.
- Practical implication: close the expectation gap first before treating this as ingestion failure.

5. Mis-qualified ESN retrieval

- Source: `mis-qualified-esn/issue`
- Main point: active ESN membership may be too broad for some retrieval decisions and may be causing a wrong document-to-ESN association.
- Practical implication: check whether region-level ESN evidence should carry more weight than the active ESN list for non-shared chunks.

6. Title vs PDF-name mismatch

- Source: `title-pdf-name-mismatch`
- Main point: the issue is noted but not yet analyzed, so this needs a first-pass fact check before prioritization can be tightened.

7. Ambiguous sections / LLM handling

- Source: `ambiguous-sections-note.md`
- Main point: some content types may be better treated as ambiguous than forced into standard section logic.
- Practical implication: this can become either a metadata design decision or a retrieval/LLM routing decision.

Suggested working order

1. Close the priority 1 section-path decision for UUID-format docs and define the affected-doc rechunk plan.
2. Resolve the QA missing-doc expectation gap and validate the mis-qualified ESN retrieval case.
3. Split format work into explicit profiles for `final_master_report` and versioned/legacy families.
4. Triage title/PDF-name mismatch and ambiguous-section handling after the higher-risk chunking and retrieval items.



